+.It Dv PROC_SYSCALL_DISPATCH_CTL
+Traps the system calls made by the calling thread, so that a program
+running foreign machine code, such as an emulator of another operating
+system, can emulate them in a
+.Dv SIGSYS
+handler.
+.Fa idtype
+must be
+.Dv P_PID
+and
+.Fa id
+must be the caller's pid or zero.
+.Fa data
+must point to a
+.Vt "struct procctl_syscall_dispatch" :
+.Bd -literal
+struct procctl_syscall_dispatch {
+	int		sd_mode;
+	int		sd_pad0;
+	uintptr_t	sd_start;
+	size_t		sd_len;
+	char		*sd_selector;
+	u_int		sd_pad1[8];
+};
+.Ed
+.Pp
+If
+.Va sd_mode
+is
+.Dv PROC_SYSCALL_DISPATCH_ON ,
+then a system call is not executed, and the thread instead receives
+.Dv SIGSYS
+with
+.Va si_code
+set to
+.Dv SYS_USER_DISPATCH ,
+.Va si_addr
+set to the address following the system call instruction and
+.Va si_syscall
+set to the system call number, unless one of the following is true:
+.Bl -bullet
+.It
+The address following the system call instruction is inside
+.Bq Va sd_start , Va sd_start No + Va sd_len .
+.It
+The system call is made by the signal trampoline in the shared page.
+.It
+.Va sd_selector
+is not
+.Dv NULL
+and the byte it points to holds
+.Dv PROC_SYSCALL_DISPATCH_ALLOW .
+Any other value, normally
+.Dv PROC_SYSCALL_DISPATCH_BLOCK ,
+traps the system call.
+The thread can flip the byte without entering the kernel.
+If the byte cannot be read, the thread receives
+.Dv SIGSEGV .
+.El
+.Pp
+The machine state is left as it was at the system call instruction,
+except that the program counter points after it, so the handler finds
+the system call number and arguments in their registers.
+If
+.Va sd_mode
+is
+.Dv PROC_SYSCALL_DISPATCH_OFF ,
+system calls are no longer trapped, and the other members must be zero.
+.Pp
+The setting is not inherited by a child created by
+.Xr fork 2
+or by new threads, and is cleared by
+.Xr execve 2 .
+It is only available to 64-bit processes.
+.It Dv PROC_SYSCALL_DISPATCH_STATUS
+Returns the syscall dispatch setting of the calling thread in the
+.Vt "struct procctl_syscall_dispatch"
+pointed to by
+.Fa data .
+.Fa idtype
+must be
+.Dv P_PID
+and
+.Fa id
+must be the caller's pid or zero.
 .It Dv PROC_TRACE_CTL
 Enable or disable tracing of the specified process(es), according to the
 value of the integer argument.
